## Build & Test

Everything runs inside the build container (via VS Code tasks / `scripts/`).
Quartus is expected to be installed on the host under `/opt/intelFPGA` and is
mounted into the container read-only. The version is selected by
`fpga.quartusBin` in `.vscode/settings.json` (default `13.0sp1`, switch to
`25.1` when needed).

```bash
# Build the container image (once):  task "Container: build image"
#   docker build --network=host -t <project>-dev .devcontainer/

# Simulate (Icarus Verilog):        task "Run tests: simulation (iverilog)"
#   iverilog -g2012 -Wall -o build/sim.vvp rtl/*.v sim/tb_blink.v && vvp build/sim.vvp

# Simulate (Quartus, VWF stimulus): tasks "Sim: Quartus functional (VWF)"
#                                   and "Sim: Quartus timing (VWF)"
#   create quartus/<project>.vwf first: Quartus GUI -> File -> New -> Vector Waveform File

# Edit pins:                        task "Pins: Pin Planner (GUI)"
#   opens the Quartus GUI on the project (Tools -> Pin Planner)

# Lint (Verilator):                 task "Static analysis: verilator"
#   verilator --lint-only -Wall rtl/*.v

# Synthesize for the FPGA:          task "Build: Quartus compile"
#   quartus_sh --flow compile <project>      (inside quartus/)

# SOF -> SVF:                       task "Build: SOF -> SVF"
#   quartus_cpf -c -q <svfClock> -g <svfVoltage> -n p output_files/<project>.sof output_files/<project>.svf
#   (both values come from .vscode/settings.json)

# Flash to the board:               task "Upload: program SRAM (SVF)"
#   openFPGALoader -c usb-blaster quartus/output_files/<project>.svf

# Full build + flash:               task "Upload: build + program (full)"
```

